WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.150
Why does this chapter matter so much?

2
00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:04.925
Because the provisioning
service is obedient.

3
00:00:04.925 --> 00:00:09.135
It owns the mapping to directory
attributes, the matching and the write,

4
00:00:09.135 --> 00:00:13.487
and Microsoft deliberately keeps the
comparison logic out of the client.

5
00:00:13.487 --> 00:00:17.010
That means everything before
the post belongs to you:

6
00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:21.013
what gets sent, in what order, how
fast, and what record you keep.

7
00:00:21.013 --> 00:00:23.312
And the endpoint is asynchronous.

8
00:00:23.312 --> 00:00:26.617
An accepted response only
means the batch was staged,

9
00:00:26.617 --> 00:00:31.349
not that anyone was written, so reading
the logs afterwards is part of the job.

10
00:00:31.349 --> 00:00:32.830
Next, which cloud.
